{"authored" [{"question" "q-132984" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate $\\lim_{z\\to1,\\ z\\ne1}f_{xyz}(-1,2,z)$ for $f(x,y,z)=x^3y^2z^2-\\frac{3}{\\ln z}$, defined on $z>0$, $z\\ne1$." "category" "mathematical_correction" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/mathematical-corrections/q-132984/review.json" "file_sha256" "fc3e428ba0613de9b1a60aaee500689a6eaa515171d5d966bb80e7169d0f9d2c" "transaction" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/mathematical-corrections/q-132984/transaction.edn" "transaction_sha256" "3b104bc9694adc5d00464b7b295b45a405d85577116f9911928bcf97a061858d" "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/mathematical-corrections/q-132984/verification.json" "basis" 2368 "rationale" "Ask explicitly for the derivative limit at the excluded point, retaining the original function and accepted value24 confirmed by live correct grade and revealed solution. The literal derivative of the original function is undefined there. Preserve the source worked solution as a prefix and append the domain clarification. Retain every field and answer identity."} {"question" "q-132984" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we find the first-order derivative ${f}_{x}(x,y,z):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{x}(x,y,z) & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({z}^{2}{x}^{3}{y}^{2}-\\frac{3}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡z}) \\\\  & =3{x}^{2}{y}^{2}{z}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we find ${f}_{xy}(x,y,z)$ by differentiating ${f}_{x}(x,y,z)$ with respect to $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{xy}(x,y,z) & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}({f}_{x}(x,y,z)) \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(3{x}^{2}{y}^{2}{z}^{2}) \\\\  & =6{x}^{2}y{z}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we find ${f}_{xyz}(x,y,z)$ by differentiating ${f}_{xy}(x,y,z)$ with respect to $z:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{xyz}(x,y,z) & =\\frac{∂}{∂z}({f}_{xy}(x,y,z)) \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂z}(6{x}^{2}y{z}^{2}) \\\\  & =12{x}^{2}yz\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate ${f}_{xyz}(x,y,z)$ at $(-1,2,1):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{xyz}(-1,2,1) & =12(-1)^{2}(2)(1)=24\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nDomain clarification: the original function is undefined at $z=1$, since $\\ln1=0$. Consequently the literal value $f_{xyz}(-1,2,1)$ in the source prompt is undefined. The derivatives above are valid on $z>0$, $z\\ne1$; there $f_x=3x^2y^2z^2$, $f_{xy}=6x^2yz^2$, and $f_{xyz}=12x^2yz$. Thus $f_{xyz}(-1,2,z)=24z$ and\n$$\\lim_{z\\to1,\\ z\\ne1}f_{xyz}(-1,2,z)=24.$$\nThe clarified study question explicitly asks for this limit, or continuous extension of the derivative, so the source's accepted answer $24$ and all original choices remain valid. This extension does not define the original function or its literal derivative at the excluded point." "category" "mathematical_correction" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/mathematical-corrections/q-132984/review.json" "file_sha256" "fc3e428ba0613de9b1a60aaee500689a6eaa515171d5d966bb80e7169d0f9d2c" "transaction" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/mathematical-corrections/q-132984/transaction.edn" "transaction_sha256" "3b104bc9694adc5d00464b7b295b45a405d85577116f9911928bcf97a061858d" "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/mathematical-corrections/q-132984/verification.json" "basis" 2368 "rationale" "Ask explicitly for the derivative limit at the excluded point, retaining the original function and accepted value24 confirmed by live correct grade and revealed solution. The literal derivative of the original function is undefined there. Preserve the source worked solution as a prefix and append the domain clarification. Retain every field and answer identity."} {"question" "q-132984" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "24"] "category" "mathematical_correction" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/mathematical-corrections/q-132984/review.json" "file_sha256" "fc3e428ba0613de9b1a60aaee500689a6eaa515171d5d966bb80e7169d0f9d2c" "transaction" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/mathematical-corrections/q-132984/transaction.edn" "transaction_sha256" "3b104bc9694adc5d00464b7b295b45a405d85577116f9911928bcf97a061858d" "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/mathematical-corrections/q-132984/verification.json" "basis" 2368 "rationale" "Ask explicitly for the derivative limit at the excluded point, retaining the original function and accepted value24 confirmed by live correct grade and revealed solution. The literal derivative of the original function is undefined there. Preserve the source worked solution as a prefix and append the domain clarification. Retain every field and answer identity."} {"question" "q-80403" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find ${f}_{xx}(x,y)+{f}_{yy}(x,y)$ given that  ${f}_{x}(x,y)=-\\frac{y}{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}$ and ${f}_{y}(x,y)=\\frac{x}{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069224/state.json" "file_sha256" "603d581b728d9f3bd0e20e9d2035c2f8e0926bb39161fad8de4d619271cbff74" "basis" 2367 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069224/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-80403" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To find ${f}_{xx}(x,y)$ we differentiate the given first-order partial derivative ${f}_{x}(x,y)$ with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{xx}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({f}_{x}(x,y)) \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(-\\frac{y}{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}) \\\\  & =-y\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}) \\\\  & =-y\\cdot (-\\frac{2x}{({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})^{2}}) \\\\  & =\\frac{2xy}{({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find ${f}_{yy}(x,y)$ we differentiate the given first-order partial derivative ${f}_{y}(x,y)$ with respect to $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{yy}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}({f}_{y}(x,y)) \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(\\frac{x}{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}) \\\\  & =x\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂y}(\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}) \\\\  & =x\\cdot (-\\frac{2y}{({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})^{2}}) \\\\  & =-\\frac{2xy}{({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{xx}(x,y)+{f}_{yy}(x,y) & =\\frac{2xy}{({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})^{2}}-\\frac{2xy}{({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})^{2}}=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069224/state.json" "file_sha256" "603d581b728d9f3bd0e20e9d2035c2f8e0926bb39161fad8de4d619271cbff74" "basis" 2367 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069224/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-80403" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069224/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "6fdf21dc036116e98209e3cdcf5e40efaae9578b69c01cb1266298703d40d6dc" "basis" 2367 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069224/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-80403" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069224/state.json" "file_sha256" "603d581b728d9f3bd0e20e9d2035c2f8e0926bb39161fad8de4d619271cbff74" "basis" 2367 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069224/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-80403" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "-\\frac{-(x+y)}{({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})^{2}}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069224/state.json" "file_sha256" "603d581b728d9f3bd0e20e9d2035c2f8e0926bb39161fad8de4d619271cbff74" "basis" 2367 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069224/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-80403" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "-\\frac{4xy}{({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})^{2}}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069224/state.json" "file_sha256" "603d581b728d9f3bd0e20e9d2035c2f8e0926bb39161fad8de4d619271cbff74" "basis" 2367 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069224/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-80403" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "-\\frac{x-y}{({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})^{2}}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069224/state.json" "file_sha256" "603d581b728d9f3bd0e20e9d2035c2f8e0926bb39161fad8de4d619271cbff74" "basis" 2367 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069224/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-80403" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "0"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069224/state.json" "file_sha256" "603d581b728d9f3bd0e20e9d2035c2f8e0926bb39161fad8de4d619271cbff74" "basis" 2367 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069224/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-80403" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{4xy}{({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})^{2}}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069224/state.json" "file_sha256" "603d581b728d9f3bd0e20e9d2035c2f8e0926bb39161fad8de4d619271cbff74" "basis" 2367 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069224/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-80469" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find ${g}_{xy}(x,y)+{g}_{xx}(x,y)$ given that  ${g}_{x}(x,y)=\\frac{x}{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069224/state.json" "file_sha256" "603d581b728d9f3bd0e20e9d2035c2f8e0926bb39161fad8de4d619271cbff74" "basis" 2367 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069224/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-80469" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To find ${g}_{xy}(x,y)$ we differentiate the given first-order partial derivative ${g}_{x}(x,y)$ with respect to $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{g}_{xy}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}({g}_{x}(x,y)) \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(\\frac{x}{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}) \\\\  & =x\\cdot (-\\frac{2y}{({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})^{2}}) \\\\  & =-\\frac{2xy}{({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find ${g}_{xx}(x,y)$ we differentiate the given first-order partial derivative ${g}_{x}(x,y)$ with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{g}_{xx}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({g}_{x}(x,y)) \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\frac{x}{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}-\\frac{x}{({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})^{2}}\\cdot 2x \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}-2{x}^{2}}{({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{{y}^{2}-{x}^{2}}{({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{g}_{xy}(x,y)+{g}_{xx}(x,y) & =-\\frac{2xy}{({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}-{x}^{2}}{({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{{y}^{2}-2xy-{x}^{2}}{({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069224/state.json" "file_sha256" "603d581b728d9f3bd0e20e9d2035c2f8e0926bb39161fad8de4d619271cbff74" "basis" 2367 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069224/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-80469" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069224/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "6fdf21dc036116e98209e3cdcf5e40efaae9578b69c01cb1266298703d40d6dc" "basis" 2367 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069224/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-80469" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069224/state.json" "file_sha256" "603d581b728d9f3bd0e20e9d2035c2f8e0926bb39161fad8de4d619271cbff74" "basis" 2367 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069224/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-80469" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{(y-x)^{2}}{({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})^{2}}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069224/state.json" "file_sha256" "603d581b728d9f3bd0e20e9d2035c2f8e0926bb39161f