e" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069224/state.json" "file_sha256" "603d581b728d9f3bd0e20e9d2035c2f8e0926bb39161fad8de4d619271cbff74" "basis" 2367 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069224/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-80469" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{{y}^{2}-2xy-{x}^{2}}{({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})^{2}}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069224/state.json" "file_sha256" "603d581b728d9f3bd0e20e9d2035c2f8e0926bb39161fad8de4d619271cbff74" "basis" 2367 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069224/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-80474" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate ${f}_{yyx}(x,y)$ given that $f(x,y)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(xy).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069224/state.json" "file_sha256" "603d581b728d9f3bd0e20e9d2035c2f8e0926bb39161fad8de4d619271cbff74" "basis" 2367 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069224/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-80474" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we find the first-order derivative ${f}_{y}(x,y):$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{y}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(xy)) \\\\  & =x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we find ${f}_{yy}(x,y)$ by differentiating ${f}_{y}(x,y)$ with respect to $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{yy}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}({f}_{y}(x,y)) \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy)) \\\\  & =-{x}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(xy)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we find ${f}_{yyx}(x,y)$ by differentiating ${f}_{yy}(x,y)$ with respect to $x:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{yyx}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({f}_{yy}(x,y)) \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(-{x}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(xy)) \\\\  & =-2x\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡(xy)-{x}^{2}\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy)\\cdot y \\\\  & =-2x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(xy)-{x}^{2}y\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy)\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069224/state.json" "file_sha256" "603d581b728d9f3bd0e20e9d2035c2f8e0926bb39161fad8de4d619271cbff74" "basis" 2367 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069224/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-80474" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069224/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "6fdf21dc036116e98209e3cdcf5e40efaae9578b69c01cb1266298703d40d6dc" "basis" 2367 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069224/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-80474" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069224/state.json" "file_sha256" "603d581b728d9f3bd0e20e9d2035c2f8e0926bb39161fad8de4d619271cbff74" "basis" 2367 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069224/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-80474" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "-2x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(xy)-{x}^{2}y\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy)"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069224/state.json" "file_sha256" "603d581b728d9f3bd0e20e9d2035c2f8e0926bb39161fad8de4d619271cbff74" "basis" 2367 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069224/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-80474" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "-x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(xy)+xy\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy)"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069224/state.json" "file_sha256" "603d581b728d9f3bd0e20e9d2035c2f8e0926bb39161fad8de4d619271cbff74" "basis" 2367 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069224/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-80474" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "-{x}^{2}y\\operatorname{sin}⁡(xy)"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069224/state.json" "file_sha256" "603d581b728d9f3bd0e20e9d2035c2f8e0926bb39161fad8de4d619271cbff74" "basis" 2367 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069224/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-80474" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "{x}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(xy)-xy\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy)"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069224/state.json" "file_sha256" "603d581b728d9f3bd0e20e9d2035c2f8e0926bb39161fad8de4d619271cbff74" "basis" 2367 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069224/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-80474" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "{x}^{2}y\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy)"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069224/state.json" "file_sha256" "603d581b728d9f3bd0e20e9d2035c2f8e0926bb39161fad8de4d619271cbff74" "basis" 2367 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069224/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-132894" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find ${g}_{xx}(x,y)-{g}_{yy}(x,y)$ at $(\\frac{\\pi }{3},\\frac{\\pi }{3})$ given that ${g}_{x}(x,y)=x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+y)-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x+y)$ and ${g}_{y}(x,y)=x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+y).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069224/state.json" "file_sha256" "603d581b728d9f3bd0e20e9d2035c2f8e0926bb39161fad8de4d619271cbff74" "basis" 2367 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069224/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-132894" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To find ${g}_{xx}(x,y)$ we differentiate the given first-order partial derivative ${g}_{x}(x,y)$ with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{g}_{xx}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({g}_{x}(x,y)) \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+y)-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x+y)) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+y)+x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x+y)+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+y) \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+y)+x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x+y)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTo find ${g}_{yy}(x,y)$ we differentiate the given first-order partial derivative ${g}_{y}(x,y)$ with respect to $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{g}_{yy}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}({g}_{y}(x,y)) \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+y)) \\\\  & =x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x+y)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nNext, we evaluate ${g}_{xx}(x,y)$ and ${g}_{yy}(x,y)$ at $(\\frac{\\pi }{3},\\frac{\\pi }{3}):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{g}_{xx}(\\frac{\\pi }{3},\\frac{\\pi }{3}) & =2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{3}+\\frac{\\pi }{3})+\\frac{\\pi }{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{3}+\\frac{\\pi }{3})=\\sqrt{3}-\\frac{\\pi }{6} \\\\ {g}_{yy}(\\frac{\\pi }{3},\\frac{\\pi }{3}) & =\\frac{\\pi }{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{3}+\\frac{\\pi }{3})=-\\frac{\\pi }{6}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we have\n\n$$\n{g}_{xx}(\\frac{\\pi }{3},\\frac{\\pi }{3})-{g}_{yy}(\\frac{\\pi }{3},\\frac{\\pi }{3})=\\sqrt{3}-\\frac{\\pi }{6}-(-\\frac{\\pi }{6})=\\sqrt{3}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069224/state.json" "file_sha256" "603d581b728d9f3bd0e20e9d2035c2f8e0926bb39161fad8de4d619271cbff74" "basis" 2367 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069224/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-132894" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069224/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "6fdf21dc036116e98209e3cdcf5e40efaae9578b69c01cb1266298703d40d6dc" "basis" 2367 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069224/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-132894" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069224/state.json" "file_sha256" "603d581b728d9f3bd0e20e9d2035c2f8e0926bb39161fad8de4d619271cbff74" "basis" 2367 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069224/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-132894" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{1}{2}(\\pi -\\sqrt{3})"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069224/state.json" "file_sha256" "603d581b728d9f3bd0e20e9d2035c2f8e0926bb39161fad8de4d619271cbff74" "basis" 2367 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069224/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-132894" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{1}{2}(\\sqrt{3}+\\pi )"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069224/state.json" "file_sha256" "603d581b728d9f3bd0e20e9d2035c2f8e0926bb39161fad8de4d619271cbff74" "basis" 2367 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069224/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-132894" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{1}{2}(\\sqrt{3}-\\frac{\\pi }{3})"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069224/state.json" "file_sha256" "603d581b728d9f3bd0e20e9d2035c2f8e0926bb39161fad8de4d619271cbff74" "basis" 2367 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069224/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-132894" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\sqrt{3}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069224/state.json" "file_sha256" "603d581b728d9f3bd0e20e9d2035c2f8e0926bb39161fad8de4d619271cbff74" "basis" 2367 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069224/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-132894" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\sqrt{3}-\\pi "] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069224/state.json" "file_sha256" "603d581b728d9f3bd0e20e9d2035c2f8e0926bb39161fad8de4d619271cbff74" "basis" 2367 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069224/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-132894" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\sqrt{3}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069224/state.json" "file_sha256" "603d581b728d9f3bd0e20e9d2035c2f8e0926bb39161fad8de4d619271cbff74" "basis" 2367 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069224/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-132984" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate ${f}_{xyz}(-1,2,1)$ for $f(x,y,z)={x}^{3}{y}^{2}{z}^{2}-\\frac{3}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡z}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069224/state.json" "file_sha256" "603d581b728d9f3bd0e20e9d2035c2f8e0926bb39161fad8de4d619271cbff74" "basis" 2367 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069224/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-132984" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we find the first-order derivative ${f}_{x}(x,y,z):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{x}(x,y,z) & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({z}^{2}{x}^{3}{y}^{2}-\\frac{3}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡z}) \\\\  & =3{x}^{2}{y}^{2}{z}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we find ${f}_{xy}(x,y,z)$ by differentiating ${f}_{x}(x,y,z)$ with respect to $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{xy}(x,y,z) & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}({f}_{x}(x,y,z)) \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(3{x}^{2}{y}^{2}{z}^{2}) \\\\  & =6{x}^{2}y{z}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we find ${f}_{xyz}(x,y,z)$ by differentiating ${f}_{xy}(x,y,z)$ with respect to $z:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{xyz}(x,y,z) & =\\frac{∂}{∂z}({f}_{xy}(x,y,z)) \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂z}(6{x}^{2}y{z}^{2}) \\\\  & =12{x}^{2}yz\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate ${f}_{xyz}(x,y,z)$ at $(-1,2,1):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{xyz}(-1,2,1) & =12(-1)^{2}(2)(1)=24\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069224/state.json" "file_sha256" "603d581b728d9f3bd0e20e9d2035c2f8e0926bb39161fad8de4d619271cbff74" "basis" 2367 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069224/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-132984" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069224/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "6fdf21dc036116e98209e3cdcf5e40efaae9578b69c01cb1266298703d40d6dc" "basis" 2367 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069224/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-132984" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069224/state.json" "file_sha256" "603d581b728d9f3bd0e20e9d2035c2f8e0926bb39161